Key Research Findings Supporting This Course

    A 12-week core stabilization program in young football players (aged 9–15) significantly improved trunk rotational parameters, lower limb loading symmetry, and reduced pain intensity from 3.33 to 2.55 on the VAS scale

    Core stability scores increase until mid-season, while ACL injury risk scores decrease with injury prevention programs that include core training

    A single bout of core stability exercises can acutely improve postural balance in soccer players with groin pain

